  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Stop 1",
      "h2": "Before money",
      "body_html": "<p class=\"big\">Before money, people used <span class=\"hl p\">barter</span> — swap goods directly.</p><p>Problem: I have eggs and you have shoes — but what if you don't want eggs? 🥚</p><p>Money fixed this. Everyone wants money.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 2",
      "h2": "Money's four jobs",
      "body_html": "<p>Money is:</p><ul><li>A <span class=\"hl p\">medium of exchange</span> — to buy.</li><li>A <span class=\"hl p\">store of value</span> — to save for later.</li><li>A <span class=\"hl p\">unit of account</span> — to compare prices.</li><li>A <b>standard of payment</b> — to pay debts.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 3",
      "h2": "Cash, card and digital",
      "body_html": "<p>Today money comes in three forms:</p><ul><li><b>Cash</b> — notes and coins.</li><li><b>Card</b> — debit or credit.</li><li><b>Digital</b> — apps, contactless, online.</li></ul><p>UK cash use is falling fast — most pay by card. 📱</p>"
    }
  ],
